		(property "Note" "Vishay LTO 50 (LTO050F10001JTE3, the BOM part; the flat footprint is dimensioned for the LTO 50 only, no alternate), 10k 5% 50 W (at 25 C case), 500 V element; up to 300 V across it and 8.9 W if the output clips at the negative rail (+/-150 V). Laid FLAT, ceramic face down in the HS1 trough (Wakefield 272-AB, bonded to GND) with non-silicone grease (Wakefield 126); leads formed like Vishay LTO 100 TB8: straight 4.2 mm from the body, inner radius 1.2 mm, 90 deg toward the ceramic side (outer lead face 6.0 +-0.5 mm from the body). M3x12 pan head + DIN125 washer through R21 / HS1 hole 1 / PCB, DIN127 + nut under the board, 0.5-0.6 Nm; screw down first, solder last. Back is isolated ceramic (1500 VRMS): no insulator. >= 1 m/s airflow across HS1 needed for any sustained DC output below about -50 V at +/-150 V (in general below +HV - 200 V); no fan needed for sine / near-0 V outputs."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "90945ced-e70d-48fb-bef1-89a65e335fbc")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
